\begin{proof}
For each quartet the direct verifier checks that the actual endpoint
product $p=(I+a)(I+e)/4$ is the orthogonal projector onto the nonsingular
line through the accepted seed $v$. Its seven supplied orbit rows have
six genuine parent edges and a right inverse of their full row matrix.
They therefore form a basis $vh_0,\ldots,vh_6$ with every $h_i$ in the
quartet subgroup $H$.

The common argument shows that the forty-nine operators
$h_i^{-1}ph_j$ span $\operatorname{End}(\mathbb F_{11}^7)$. Hence $H$
acts irreducibly. For the table's word $W$ the verifier also checks
$Y=W^6\ne I$ and $Y^{37}=I$, so $H$ contains an element of order $37$.
If $H$ were proper in $G_2(11)$, the borrowed complete maximal subgroup
theorem would place it in a natural unitary normalizer preserving a
rational line. This contradicts irreducibility.
\end{proof}

